{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1117930-make-the-haven-merit-great-again","id":1117930,"title":"Make the Haven Merit Great Again","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-18T14:27:38-07:00","id":1117930,"title":"Make the Haven Merit Great Again","content":"So Safe place and Haven is kinda like the middle child of merits in most of our games. It's usually bought by at least on player but beyond a comfortable place to stay it 's just not worth it. It gives you extra dice to safety and waking when attacked and blood smells extra good inside your comfort zone.<br /> And for this you\u2019ll have to pay for 2 merits, sure you only need 1 dot in Safe Place, but the first dot in haven is twice as expensive as other things you want.<br /> <br /> This is really good, and i give them that. It is just that this is almost never good in our chronicles, attacking the PCs during the day in their home is just a booring dick move. And beyond, our games are usually never really violent. <br /> <br /> So for our group, Haven is really subpar with other merits but it fills themes and gives mood and personality to the characters. So I\u2019m looking for other things the Merit could do either instead of what it does or add to it to make it worthwhile.<br /> <br /> <br /> PS. I don\u2019t need to hear \u201dhow good it is\u201d, because we all know that, it\u2019s just not useful in our playstyle DS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T15:08:39-07:00","id":1117947,"title":"","content":"Put a largely useless and overly expensive wall around it? I kid, I kid.<br /> <br /> Ditch the safe place requirement, make haven work without it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T15:09:33-07:00","id":1117948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1117930-make-the-haven-merit-great-again#post1117930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is really good, and i give them that. It is just that this is almost never good in our chronicles, attacking the PCs during the day in their home is just a booring dick move. And beyond, our games are usually never really violent.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this case you might as well just skip it, everyone gets a home or place to live. It's basically an out-of-game thing at that point, there's no reason to charge them for it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T15:13:51-07:00","id":1117950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1117930-make-the-haven-merit-great-again?p=1117947#post1117947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Put a largely useless and overly expensive wall around it? I kid, I kid.</div> </div> </div> </div>And make the Storyteller pay for it. :P<br /> <br /> Anyways, on a more serious note - you could have your haven tied to a particular merit and grant bonuses for that merit while at the haven? Similar to how wolf did territory in 1e. Bonuses to computers for a hacker tend to be good - or, if say you had bonuses to persuasion I could see a vampire literally -bringing- people to their haven (for all the dangers that has). Or you could make Haven and safe place the same merit for vampires, and tie to to like... feeding grounds or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T15:23:04-07:00","id":1117955,"title":"","content":"You're going to have to be a bit more specific. You don't like doing Safe Place invasions. Cool, cool. That's fine. But what is relevant to your game? Social bonuses (well, that's kind of Ordo wyrm nest stuff too)? Territory awareness? The ability to make rules over your home that's considered Law by the Kindred?<br /> <br /> As others have suggested, you could just drop the merit too. There's lots of other territory merits that you could look at instead - feeding ground, wyrm nest, mandragora garden, the temple one, library, etc that reflect one's home. You don't need to call a merit &quot;haven&quot; to be part of a haven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-18-2017, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T15:35:57-07:00","id":1117961,"title":"","content":"In Requrim 1e Haven was 3 merits, Size, Location and Security now Location is Feeding Grounds, Security is Safe Place and Haven exists as it's own merit possibly because it was felt it had to be included (I said possibly, let's not argue hypotheticals) so what's missing is Haven Size.<br /> I would hazard a guess that what your group wants is a place where they can play host and aren't finding it in the merit so they aren't taking it, in this case a Status merit or Resources to justify a big home can give them what they are looking for. Another posable answer is the group just don't think it maters where they live therefore aren't interested by spending xp to represent it.<br /> Is it always the same player who buys Haven in each game? It may be that they are just more motivated to have a safe guard against unexpected attacks than the rest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T15:39:52-07:00","id":1117964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">In this case you might as well just skip it, everyone gets a home or place to live. It's basically an out-of-game thing at that point, there's no reason to charge them for it. </span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><br /> Yeah i don't think it's the intent of the game that you don't have a place to sleep without safe place so already there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyways, on a more serious note - you could have your haven tied to a particular merit and grant bonuses for that merit while at the haven? Similar to how wolf did territory in 1e. Bonuses to computers for a hacker tend to be good - or, if say you had bonuses to persuasion I could see a vampire literally -bringing- people to their haven (for all the dangers that has). Or you could make Haven and safe place the same merit for vampires, and tie to to like... feeding grounds or something. </div> </div> </div>Im not really familiar with W:tF 1ed, could you explain a bit deeper. Skillz bonuses is nice, maybe something like giving 8-again or +2 or something to a number of skills equal to haven dots. I like the implications there, bringing people to your haven for bonuses to skill rolls, that can give some nice drama.<br /> Smashing Haven together with Feeding Grounds would be a decent idea as well, however not without serious consequences for the domain politics and such. You can't really have you secluded family estate in the middle of nowhere then. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're going to have to be a bit more specific. You don't like doing Safe Place invasions. Cool, cool. That's fine. But what is relevant to your game? Social bonuses (well, that's kind of Ordo wyrm nest stuff too)? Territory awareness? The ability to make rules over your home that's considered Law by the Kindred? </div> </div> </div>I guess we're pretty much into social and political play, a balance of drama, politics and character relations. Social bonuses, mental bonuses and such. The wyrm nests merits are really nice so something similar to that would work. My players also really like to try to take control and make sure to secure and get a powerbase in their feeding grounds (not necessary tied to the merit).<br /> Hmm yeah i've always taken for granted that &quot;your home, your rules&quot;, but binding that to Haven could be a thing. Perhaps not mysticly binding, but perhaps something like need to spend a WP to break the rules, or consider your city status to be higher in your Haven.<br /> <br /> Even like the possibility to regain willpower in your sleep is an idea i just got. Maybe tied to Humanity as well. Like roll you merit dots in Haven - the social penalty from relating to humans. If successful, you regain a point of Willpower in your sleep as if alive.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> </span><br /> </span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T15:46:22-07:00","id":1117967,"title":"","content":"I might be thinking of damnation city too. *tries to remember* Anyways, one of the books had locations that were rated 1-5 that granted equipment bonuses for a particular skill because of all the tools it had for that skill within it. Something rated 5 in medicine might be a well off hospital with all the tools to perform surgery or what have you. A place dedicated to persuasion might always be filled with a particular scent, be well kept, and inviting - and always seem to have the perfect mood music while you talk to a person. A place tied to the occult might have a ritual circle and be set atop an intersection of leylines (and may or may not be the target of various supernaturals...) My recommendation would be to allow people to basically fill their haven with these kinds of equipment bonuses to represent how well kept or stocked it is on top of Haven's usual benefits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T15:51:14-07:00","id":1117972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In Requrim 1e Haven was 3 merits, Size, Location and Security now Location is Feeding Grounds, Security is Safe Place and Haven exists as it's own merit possibly because it was felt it had to be included (I said possibly, let's not argue hypotheticals) so what's missing is Haven Size.<br /> I would hazard a guess that what your group wants is a place where they can play host and aren't finding it in the merit so they aren't taking it, in this case a Status merit or Resources to justify a big home can give them what they are looking for. Another posable answer is the group just don't think it maters where they live therefore aren't interested by spending xp to represent it.<br /> Is it always the same player who buys Haven in each game? It may be that they are just more motivated to have a safe guard against unexpected attacks than the rest. </div> </div> </div><br /> Nah, not really. Like You always get a home that's fitting your social class and background, but you don't really get any mechanical benefits unless you buy it with exp. Big fancy apartment is okay if your playing someone in the higher ups of society. However, security comes from Safe Place and fancy equipment bonus to social rolls and such comes from resources. But most of them justify big fancy homes with resources, status, mentor etc. They do however usually care about their place to live, unless they play a character that really doesn't, but that's rare. <br /> And no, it's a mix of players, usually depending if they want a little bit extra protection, they feel paranoid or they just really think it would fit their character to live in a place that's safer then most.<br /> <br /> It's usually what fits the character that the player buys, non of my players are into power-gaming or such. <br /> <br /> I want something to make Haven more interesting and more worthwhile to buy, and not be just , well 2 or 3 experience wasted on nothing except character concept. ( I don't mean that's a waste, but if it's just for that and never used in play, you could have it for free IMHO)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T15:54:27-07:00","id":1117973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1117930-make-the-haven-merit-great-again?p=1117967#post1117967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might be thinking of damnation city too. *tries to remember* Anyways, one of the books had locations that were rated 1-5 that granted equipment bonuses for a particular skill because of all the tools it had for that skill within it. Something rated 5 in medicine might be a well off hospital with all the tools to perform surgery or what have you. A place dedicated to persuasion might always be filled with a particular scent, be well kept, and inviting - and always seem to have the perfect mood music while you talk to a person. A place tied to the occult might have a ritual circle and be set atop an intersection of leylines (and may or may not be the target of various supernaturals...) My recommendation would be to allow people to basically fill their haven with these kinds of equipment bonuses to represent how well kept or stocked it is on top of Haven's usual benefits.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh yeah that seems familiar. I think it's Sites in Damnation City, they work ( at least how i remember it) like that. That is a really nice and simple solution actually. Let the players design their haven with skill-modifiers in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T18:21:16-07:00","id":1118016,"title":"","content":"Rather than come up with extra effects, our table just made the Merit cheaper. We made Haven a one-dot Merit. You attach the Haven Merit to a Single Safe Place. The Haven Rating is equal to the Rating of the Safe Place it is attached to. If you buy multiple Safe Places, you can can buy additional Haven merits to attach to those. Oh, and for Communal Havens, multiple Kindred could attach their Haven merit to the same Safe Place.<br /> <br /> People were willing to spend an extra <i>dot </i>on haven, but an <i>extra dot</i> <i>per safe place pip</i> was asking a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T05:09:25-07:00","id":1118133,"title":"","content":"Using Sites and one Skill bonus as 'character special Haven' looks very nice. I imagine all those 'special libraries' of Ordo Dracul, ritual chambers of Circe of Crone or churches that improve Persuasion (?) for Lancea Sanctum! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T09:46:59-07:00","id":1118196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1117930-make-the-haven-merit-great-again?p=1117964#post1117964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah i don't think it's the intent of the game that you don't have a place to sleep without safe place so already there.<br /> <br /> ... need to spend a WP to break the rules, or consider your city status to be higher in your Haven.<br /> <br /> Even like the possibility to regain willpower in your sleep is an idea i just got. Maybe tied to Humanity as well. Like roll you merit dots in Haven - the social penalty from relating to humans. If successful, you regain a point of Willpower in your sleep as if alive.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I was going to just post how delighted I was to see such an elegant and effective solution to two problems at once (haven merit value and the daily Willpower issue). But, there are some structured contributions I can throw out as framework suggestions....<br /> <br /> <b>Haven (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <u>Prerequisite: </u>Safe Place \u2022<br /> <u>Effect:</u> A good haven is not only safe from the sun, but also familiar and comforting. The dot rating reflects your character\u2019s affinity for his home and its defenses against the sun\u2019s intrusion.<br /> A low rating might be poorly sealed, undecorated and subject to distractions whenever the neighbors wake. A high rating might imply an ancestral home with subterranean vaults furnished through the work of generations to considerable ambiance.<br /> Haven dots provide several benefits:<br /> * Add your Haven dots to any Humanity rolls to notice danger while sleeping;<br /> * Add Haven dots to any rolls to remain awake (Stamina + Resolve) .<br /> * Similarly, add it to any Kindred senses (see p. 90) rolls within.<br /> * Further, you may roll your merit dots in dice to regain 1 Willpower whenever you sleep in your Haven.<br /> * Select one skill specialty for each dot of Haven. Exercise of a designated specialty within your haven benefits from the 9-again quality, or if already possessed, the 8-again quality. If the 8-again quality is already possessed the specialty may be exercised as a rote action.<br /> <u>Drawback:</u> Losing a Haven is a breaking point at Humanity 8, minus its dot rating. A Haven must be tied to a Safe Place Merit (see p. 123). Like a Safe Place, a coterie may share a Haven Merit. Each member that wishes to benefit must invest Merit dots in both the Safe Place and the Haven. Should you roll a critical failure while attempting to regain Willpower sleeping in your Haven, reduce your Haven rating by 1 dot (subject to Sanctity of Merits)--something feels off and will require re-arrangement and investment of your time to correct.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Haven of Clay</b> <b>(\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> &quot;<i>Let the other clans wrestle and strain with esoteric riddles of what it is to be a monster. They need havens, an audience, solitude, mortal institutions, or secrets. The Gangrel take what they want. All that they need is locked away in the endless potential of their horrific clay.</i>&quot; (VtR 2e p. 17)<br /> <u>Effect:</u> You have embraced the independence of the Gangrel clan and your haven is the dirt or other substance you sleep in, your Unmarked Grave. While you slumber, the flesh of the earth comforts you the same way the gentle embrace of a mother's womb comforts a child waiting to burst forth into the world. You may roll your merit dots in dice to regain 1 Willpower whenever you sleep in your Unmarked Grave.<br /> <u>Drawback:</u> However on a critical failure you lose 1 Willpower to nightmares and the lingering desire to remain much longer.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12493,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","user":"Khanwulf","date":". 07-19-2017, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T11:36:13-07:00","id":1118225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1117930-make-the-haven-merit-great-again?p=1118196#post1118196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was going to just post how delighted I was to see such and elegant and effective solution to two problems at once (haven merit value and the daily Willpower issue). But, there are some structured contributions I can throw out as framework suggestions....<br /> <br /> <b>Haven (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <u>Prerequisite: </u>Safe Place \u2022<br /> <u>Effect:</u> A good haven is not only safe from the sun, but also familiar and comforting. The dot rating reflects your character\u2019s affinity for his home and its defenses against the sun\u2019s intrusion.<br /> A low rating might be poorly sealed, undecorated and subject to distractions whenever the neighbors wake. A high rating might imply an ancestral home with subterranean vaults furnished through the work of generations to considerable ambiance.<br /> Haven dots provide several benefits:<br /> * Add your Haven dots to any Humanity rolls to notice danger while sleeping;<br /> * Add Haven dots to any rolls to remain awake (Stamina + Resolve) .<br /> * Similarly, add it to any Kindred senses (see p. 90) rolls within.<br /> * Further, you may roll your merit dots in dice to regain 1 Willpower whenever you sleep in your Haven.<br /> * Select one skill specialty for each dot of Haven. Exercise of a designated specialty within your haven benefits from the 9-again quality, or if already possessed, the 8-again quality. If the 8-again quality is already possessed the specialty may be exercised as a rote action.<br /> <u>Drawback:</u> Losing a Haven is a breaking point at Humanity 8, minus its dot rating. A Haven must be tied to a Safe Place Merit (see p. 123). Like a Safe Place, a coterie may share a Haven Merit. Each member that wishes to benefit must invest Merit dots in both the Safe Place and the Haven. Should you roll a critical failure while attempting to regain Willpower sleeping in your Haven, reduce your Haven rating by 1 dot (subject to Sanctity of Merits)--something feels off and will require re-arrangement and investment of your time to correct.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Haven of Clay</b> <b>(\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> &quot;<i>Let the other clans wrestle and strain with esoteric riddles of what it is to be a monster. They need havens, an audience, solitude, mortal institutions, or secrets. The Gangrel take what they want. All that they need is locked away in the endless potential of their horrific clay.</i>&quot; (VtR 2e p. 17)<br /> <u>Effect:</u> You have embraced the independence of the Gangrel clan and your haven is the dirt or other substance you sleep in, your Unmarked Grave. While you slumber, the flesh of the earth comforts you the same way the gentle embrace of a mother's womb comforts a child waiting to burst forth into the world. You may roll your merit dots in dice to regain 1 Willpower whenever you sleep in your Unmarked Grave.<br /> <u>Drawback:</u> However on a critical failure you lose 1 Willpower to nightmares and the lingering desire to remain much longer.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I. Love. This. !<br /> <br /> Thanks for putting our ideas into usable text! And the addition of that Gangrel / Protean merit, beautiful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T12:47:08-07:00","id":1118245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1117930-make-the-haven-merit-great-again?p=1118225#post1118225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I. Love. This. !<br /> <br /> Thanks for putting our ideas into usable text! And the addition of that Gangrel / Protean merit, beautiful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pleased as always to be of service.<br /> <br /> Things of note: if you have a group haven they'll have to decide together for which specialties it is optimized. Some might want research-focused ones (taking advantage of daytime puttering investigations), others more physical specialties. I can imagine a haven optimized for swords, for example; fear invading that one! (This is why the Carthians just firebomb you, after all....)<br /> <br /> Haven of Clay is the result of searching for &quot;Haven&quot; on the PDF and going... Oh. Oh yeah. Gangrel.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T14:24:24-07:00","id":1118277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1117930-make-the-haven-merit-great-again?p=1118245#post1118245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pleased as always to be of service.<br /> <br /> Things of note: if you have a group haven they'll have to decide together for which specialties it is optimized. Some might want research-focused ones (taking advantage of daytime puttering investigations), others more physical specialties. I can imagine a haven optimized for swords, for example; fear invading that one! (This is why the Carthians just firebomb you, after all....)<br /> <br /> Haven of Clay is the result of searching for &quot;Haven&quot; on the PDF and going... Oh. Oh yeah. Gangrel.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>Any ideas for the other Clans/Disciplines? Like a Den of Decadence lulling guests/Invaders into complacency for Majesty? Or a Pit of Nightmares for sowing terror (perhaps even after individuals have left)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T08:22:16-07:00","id":1118568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1117930-make-the-haven-merit-great-again?p=1118277#post1118277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any ideas for the other Clans/Disciplines? Like a Den of Decadence lulling guests/Invaders into complacency for Majesty? Or a Pit of Nightmares for sowing terror (perhaps even after individuals have left)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll think about it. However please note that the bonus to specialization use represents both the great familiarity of your home AND a certain customization to your own tastes--an expression of your preferences to your own benefit and potentially thereby the detriment of &quot;visitors&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, if you're a Daeva delighted by decadent entertainment and decor, you'll select as your 1 (or more) Haven specializations affected one that works with your skills specialization for seduction and the like.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> I actually see the point here. You're thinking about Discipline use, while the framework above is specific to SKILL use. Ok. My first inclination is &quot;if the Haven is supernaturally attuned to help with Disciplines/Devotions that had better be another Merit!&quot; Will consider possible recommendations. Perhaps like wyrm nest bonuses?<br /> <br /> Gangrel get a Haven-merit replacement because they often don't even have a traditional haven, per se. They just sink into the ground wherever, and are cool with that.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}